# Local-only reference clones, NOT part of this repo.
#
# These patterns are ANCHORED with a leading `/` on purpose. binaryen-ts carried
# an unanchored `wabt-ts/` here to ignore its sibling checkout, which was correct
# in that repo and became a trap in this one: after the merge it matched
# src/wabt-ts/, tests/wabt-ts/, scripts/wabt-ts/ and cmem/wabt-ts/ -- half the
# merged tree. Already-tracked files were unaffected, so nothing looked wrong,
# but every NEW file on the wabt side would have been silently untracked, and
# deno fmt/lint skipped those directories entirely.
#
# wabt-ts's own version anchored the same intent (`/binaryen-ts/`, `/upstream/`)
# and would have survived the merge untouched. Anchor anything that names a
# directory rather than a kind of file.
/upstream/
/wasmtk/
